course: dictionary
lesson: 1042
title: Boreal: the cold northern forest
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Boreal is a word for the cold north. It describes the far north, near the Arctic, and the forests that grow there.
explain: The clues in the sentence help you. «The taiga, or boreal forest, is mostly spruce, pine, fir and larch.» The word "or" tells you that taiga and boreal forest mean the same thing here.
explain: Other words around boreal give more clues: cold, winters, spruce and pine all point to the north. Try swapping in "northern" for boreal. The sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Boreal means of the far north, near the Arctic.
fact: The boreal forest is a belt of cold northern forest full of conifer trees, such as spruce, pine and fir.
fact: The boreal forest stretches across Canada, Alaska, Scandinavia and Russia.
fact: «The taiga, or boreal forest, is mostly spruce, pine, fir and larch.»
fact: The boreal forest is the world's largest land biome, with long, cold winters and short summers.
exercise: In «The taiga, or boreal forest, is mostly spruce, pine, fir and larch», what does boreal forest mean? | A city park | A warm desert | A tropical rainforest by the sea | *The cold northern forest of conifer trees
exercise: Which word in «The taiga, or boreal forest» tells you that taiga and boreal forest mean the same thing? | *or | and | is | mostly
exercise: Which animal can you find in the boreal forest? | Kangaroo | *Lynx | Penguin | Camel
test: Which of these is a clue that a place is boreal? | *Long, cold winters | Palm trees | Hot sand dunes | Coral reefs
test: Boreal means which of these? | Hot and dry | *Of the far north, near the Arctic | Under the sea | Near the equator
exam: What is the best swap for boreal in «boreal forest» if you want to check your meaning? | Tropical | *Northern | Southern | Hot
